\f1\i\b SESSION-4 ASSIGNMENT\
(1)ALL 6 PHASES OF SDLC:\
(1)Requirement Analysis:
\f2\b0 Gather and understand the project requirements.\

\f1\b (2)Planning:
\f2\b0 Plan the project timeline,budget,and resources.\

\f1\b (3)Design:
\f2\b0 Create the software architecture and design.\

\f1\b (4)Development:
\f2\b0 Write the code to build the software.\

\f1\b (5)Testing:
\f2\b0 Test the software to find and fix bugs.\

\f1\b (6)Maintenance:
\f2\b0 Release the software and maintain it with updates and fixes.\
\

\f1\b (2)DIFFERENCE BETWEEN AGILE AND WATERFALL MODELS:\
AGILE:\

\f2\b0 .Development is done in small iterations.\
.Changes can be made during the project.\
.Customer feedback is taken regularly.\
\

\f1\b WATERFALL:
\f2\b0 \
.Development is done in one sequence.\
.Changes are difficult after development starts.\
.Customer feedback is usually taken at the end.\
\

\f1\b (3)3 main scrum roles and one line about each:\
.Product Owner:
\f2\b0 Defines the product requirements and priorities.
\f1\b \
.Scrum Master:
\f2\b0 Helps the team follow scrum practices and removes obstacles.\

\f1\b .Development Team:
\f2\b0 Designs,develops,and tests the product.\
\

\f1\b (4)SPRINT IN SCRUM AND ITS DURATION:\

\f2\b0 .A Sprint is a fixed period during which is the scrum team completes a set of tasks.\
.Typical duration:1 to 4 weeks(most commonly 2 weeks)\
\

\f1\b (5)JIRA BOARD COLUMNS MEAN:\
.Backlog:
\f2\b0 List of tasks that are planned but not started.\

\f1\b .To Do:
\f2\b0 Tasks ready to begin.\

\f1\b .In Progess:
\f2\b0 Tasks currently being worked on.\

\f1\b .Done:
\f2\b0 Tasks that have been completed.}